post_install() {
    cat <<'MSG'

Bluetooth (iPhone messages and notifications) needs one-time system setup.

tether-btclass@.service is installed but NOT enabled. Enabling it changes how
this machine presents itself over Bluetooth, so that is your call to make.

Notification mirroring also needs a bluetooth.service drop-in, likewise not
applied for you. Apply it BEFORE pairing an iPhone: a bond made without it has
no LE half.

To see exactly what is left, and the commands to run:

    tether --bt-setup

WiFi needs inbound 5134/tcp, and 5353/udp for mDNS discovery. Profiles for ufw
and firewalld are installed but NOT applied, for the same reason:

    sudo ufw allow Tether
    sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --add-service=tether && sudo firewall-cmd --reload

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
    post_install
}
